    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/listing/": {
      "title": "Explore Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Explore Careers | Working at Quinnipiac University Search is currently not available. A Quinnipiac Education Academics Undergraduate Graduate Medicine Law Apply Now Visit Contact Us Life at Quinnipiac Student Experience Quinnipiac Now Athletics & Recreation Admissions Admissions Apply Now Tuition & Financial Aid Meet Us Visit Us Virtual Tour Contact Us On Campus Maps & Directions Our Campuses University Calendar University Directory About Quinnipiac Explore Videos Student Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog University Policies Health & Campus Safety Course Finder MyQ Other Resources Alumni Career Development Office Institutes & Centers Ireland's Great Hunger Museum Make a Tuition Payment News Media Parents QCard Quinnipiac University Online Quinnipiac University Poll Quinnipiac Magazine Request a Transcript Student Consumer Information WQUN Working at Quinnipiac Schools Arts & Sciences Business Communications Education Engineering Health Sciences Law Medicine Nursing Looking for a specific program? Program Listing Dual-Degree Programs Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Carret icon Explore Careers Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Application Process Benefits Community Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great. We can send you jobs like this. if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search Results Position Campus Closes Associate Director of High School Partnerships & Pre-College Recruitment Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University invites applications for the position of Associate Director of High School Partnerships and Pre-College Recruitment. Reporting to the Dean of Admissions and Financial Aid, this role supports the execution and coordination of a unified strategy for engaging high school students, counselors, and partner schools across multiple pre-college pathways.\n\nThe Associate Director plays a central role in managing the “front end” of the pre-college pipeline—including summer programs and dual/concurrent enrollment—ensuring a coordinated approach to recruitment, inquiry management, and conversion. This position serves as a key liaison across Admissions, Lifelong Learning, Strategic Programs & Partnerships, and the academic schools and colleges to align outreach, communications, and partnership development. Full-Time Faculty: Health and Exercise Science (Nutrition) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University’s Department of Health and Exercise Science, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for a full-time, 12-month position at the Assistant Professor rank (Tenure-Track or Clinical Track) in the area of human nutrition. Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Quinnipiac University's School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science at the Department of Diagnostic Imaging.  This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful difference in the lives of future healthcare professionals while working in a collaborative and dynamic university environment. Director of Digital Content Strategy Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The ideal candidate is experienced in analyzing performance in SEO/AEO/GEO, understands how to improve it, and provides best-practice-based content creation recommendations to our marketing and communications development teams. The position will guide storytelling across platforms and ensure content is engaging and discoverable. Executive Director of Simulation North Haven - North Haven, CT As the inaugural Executive Director of Simulation, this individual will collaboratively facilitate the establishment of the overall enterprise structure of a Quinnipiac University immersive practice and collaborative training center from the ground up, including its organizational design, operations, policies, and procedures. This foundational work will set the framework for how the center functions, scales, and integrates across the university for years to come. Assistant Director of Residential Life York Hill - Hamden, CT Reporting directly to the Director of Residential Life, the Assistant Director serves as an integral member of the department's senior leadership team and provides oversight for a residential community of approximately 1,600 first-year students. Armed Public Safety Officer Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Under the direction of Quinnipiac University's Chief of Public Safety, we invite applications for the position of Armed Public Safety Officer. This is an opportunity to join the university to protect and provide a safe and secure environment for our students, faculty, staff, and visitors. As an Armed Public Safety Officer, you will serve as a liaison and a resource to local law enforcement as needed.  \n\nWe offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Residence Hall Director York Hill - Hamden, CT Residence Hall Directors serve as key student affairs professionals within the Division of Student Affairs and are responsible for fostering community development, supporting student wellness, responding to student concerns, and enhancing the residential student experience through leadership, mentorship, education, and crisis response. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Philosophy (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The Department of Philosophy and Political Science in the College of Arts & Sciences at Quinnipiac University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The preferred start date is January 2027 or August 2027. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Assistant Professor) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The School of Business at Quinnipiac University invites dynamic, innovative, and student-focused educators to join our Finance Department as a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Finance beginning in Fall 2027. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Associate Professor) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University's School of Business  seeks a faculty member who can contribute not only through excellence in teaching and scholarship, but also through leadership in program development, faculty collaboration, industry engagement, and strategic initiatives. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Legal Studies-Emerging Legal Technologies & Civil Procedures (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses, including Civil Procedures, as well as courses aligned with their expertise and program needs. We have a strong preference for candidates with experience teaching and researching innovative and emerging legal technologies, such as artificial intelligence (AI), and who can enhance our curriculum accordingly. Licensed Mechanic - HVAC Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The HVAC Mechanic position is responsible for performing highly skilled and skilled maintenance on Quinnipiac University buildings, property, or related buildings. Assistant Women's Softball Coach Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT This position will assist in program management including coaching, administration, recruitment and coordination of a collegiate Women’s Softball program. Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Quinnipiac University’s School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, 12-month year-round Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work This is an exciting opportunity to join a rapidly growing Master of Social Work (MSW) program committed to preparing competent, socially responsive social workers through flexible, high-quality learning environments. Project Manager, Strategic Plan Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Reporting to the Chief of Staff with a dotted line to the President, the Project Manager, Strategic Plan will serve as the University's central coordinator for implementation. This individual will work closely with the President, Management Committee, Strategy Team sponsors, Finance, and other institutional partners to keep initiatives moving, decisions organized, and implementation work coordinated across academic and administrative areas. Public Safety Officer Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University invites applications for the position of Public Safety Officer. Under the direction of the Chief of Public Safety, reporting directly to an assigned Public Safety Sergeant, the Public Safety Officer, shall provide a safe and secure environment for faculty, staff, students and guests of the University while protecting the assets of the University. Residence Hall Director Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Residence Hall Directors serve as key student affairs professionals within the Division of Student Affairs and are responsible for fostering community development, supporting student wellness, responding to student concerns, and enhancing the residential student experience through leadership, mentorship, education, and crisis response. Associate Provost, Executive Director of Career Development Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT This is a unique opportunity to shape the future of career education and experiential learning at a university committed to preparing students not only for their first job, but for meaningful, adaptable, and purpose-driven careers. Business Operations Manager Whitney Avenue - Hamden, CT This role is responsible for managing and overseeing the department’s financial operations, , operational processes to support strategic growth and serving as liaison with the Office of Human Resources for department personnel related matters. More Jobs 22 Position Campus Closes Associate Director of High School Partnerships & Pre-College Recruitment Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University invites applications for the position of Associate Director of High School Partnerships and Pre-College Recruitment. Reporting to the Dean of Admissions and Financial Aid, this role supports the execution and coordination of a unified strategy for engaging high school students, counselors, and partner schools across multiple pre-college pathways.\n\nThe Associate Director plays a central role in managing the “front end” of the pre-college pipeline—including summer programs and dual/concurrent enrollment—ensuring a coordinated approach to recruitment, inquiry management, and conversion. This position serves as a key liaison across Admissions, Lifelong Learning, Strategic Programs & Partnerships, and the academic schools and colleges to align outreach, communications, and partnership development. Full-Time Faculty: Health and Exercise Science (Nutrition) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University’s Department of Health and Exercise Science, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for a full-time, 12-month position at the Assistant Professor rank (Tenure-Track or Clinical Track) in the area of human nutrition. Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Quinnipiac University's School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science at the Department of Diagnostic Imaging.  This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful difference in the lives of future healthcare professionals while working in a collaborative and dynamic university environment. Director of Digital Content Strategy Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The ideal candidate is experienced in analyzing performance in SEO/AEO/GEO, understands how to improve it, and provides best-practice-based content creation recommendations to our marketing and communications development teams. The position will guide storytelling across platforms and ensure content is engaging and discoverable. Executive Director of Simulation North Haven - North Haven, CT As the inaugural Executive Director of Simulation, this individual will collaboratively facilitate the establishment of the overall enterprise structure of a Quinnipiac University immersive practice and collaborative training center from the ground up, including its organizational design, operations, policies, and procedures. This foundational work will set the framework for how the center functions, scales, and integrates across the university for years to come. Assistant Director of Residential Life York Hill - Hamden, CT Reporting directly to the Director of Residential Life, the Assistant Director serves as an integral member of the department's senior leadership team and provides oversight for a residential community of approximately 1,600 first-year students. Armed Public Safety Officer Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Under the direction of Quinnipiac University's Chief of Public Safety, we invite applications for the position of Armed Public Safety Officer. This is an opportunity to join the university to protect and provide a safe and secure environment for our students, faculty, staff, and visitors. As an Armed Public Safety Officer, you will serve as a liaison and a resource to local law enforcement as needed.  \n\nWe offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Residence Hall Director York Hill - Hamden, CT Residence Hall Directors serve as key student affairs professionals within the Division of Student Affairs and are responsible for fostering community development, supporting student wellness, responding to student concerns, and enhancing the residential student experience through leadership, mentorship, education, and crisis response. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Philosophy (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The Department of Philosophy and Political Science in the College of Arts & Sciences at Quinnipiac University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The preferred start date is January 2027 or August 2027. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Assistant Professor) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The School of Business at Quinnipiac University invites dynamic, innovative, and student-focused educators to join our Finance Department as a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Finance beginning in Fall 2027. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Associate Professor) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University's School of Business  seeks a faculty member who can contribute not only through excellence in teaching and scholarship, but also through leadership in program development, faculty collaboration, industry engagement, and strategic initiatives. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Legal Studies-Emerging Legal Technologies & Civil Procedures (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses, including Civil Procedures, as well as courses aligned with their expertise and program needs. We have a strong preference for candidates with experience teaching and researching innovative and emerging legal technologies, such as artificial intelligence (AI), and who can enhance our curriculum accordingly. Licensed Mechanic - HVAC Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The HVAC Mechanic position is responsible for performing highly skilled and skilled maintenance on Quinnipiac University buildings, property, or related buildings. Assistant Women's Softball Coach Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT This position will assist in program management including coaching, administration, recruitment and coordination of a collegiate Women’s Softball program. Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Quinnipiac University’s School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, 12-month year-round Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work This is an exciting opportunity to join a rapidly growing Master of Social Work (MSW) program committed to preparing competent, socially responsive social workers through flexible, high-quality learning environments. Project Manager, Strategic Plan Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Reporting to the Chief of Staff with a dotted line to the President, the Project Manager, Strategic Plan will serve as the University's central coordinator for implementation. This individual will work closely with the President, Management Committee, Strategy Team sponsors, Finance, and other institutional partners to keep initiatives moving, decisions organized, and implementation work coordinated across academic and administrative areas. Public Safety Officer Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University invites applications for the position of Public Safety Officer. Under the direction of the Chief of Public Safety, reporting directly to an assigned Public Safety Sergeant, the Public Safety Officer, shall provide a safe and secure environment for faculty, staff, students and guests of the University while protecting the assets of the University. Residence Hall Director Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Residence Hall Directors serve as key student affairs professionals within the Division of Student Affairs and are responsible for fostering community development, supporting student wellness, responding to student concerns, and enhancing the residential student experience through leadership, mentorship, education, and crisis response. Associate Provost, Executive Director of Career Development Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT This is a unique opportunity to shape the future of career education and experiential learning at a university committed to preparing students not only for their first job, but for meaningful, adaptable, and purpose-driven careers. Business Operations Manager Whitney Avenue - Hamden, CT This role is responsible for managing and overseeing the department’s financial operations, , operational processes to support strategic growth and serving as liaison with the Office of Human Resources for department personnel related matters. More Jobs 22 Powered by PageUp Already Applied? Complete your application, submit your application, or view the status of an application. Login Search Refine Search Type Full-time 30 Part-time 12 Campus Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT 32 North Haven - North Haven, CT 6 Whitney Avenue - Hamden, CT 1 York Hill - Hamden, CT 3 Categories Faculty 18 Staff 24 Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Quinnipiac Home About Quinnipiac https://www.facebook.com/QuinnipiacUniversity http://twitter.com/quinnipiacu https://instagram.com/quinnipiacu © 2020 Quinnipiac University. All Rights Reserved. Website Security and Privacy Policy Legal Info"
