 difference in the lives of future healthcare professionals while working in a collaborative and dynamic university environment. Full-Time Faculty: Health and Exercise Science (Nutrition) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University’s Department of Health and Exercise Science, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for a full-time, 12-month position at the Assistant Professor rank (Tenure-Track or Clinical Track) in the area of human nutrition. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Assistant Professor) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The School of Business at Quinnipiac University invites dynamic, innovative, and student-focused educators to join our Finance Department as a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Finance beginning in Fall 2027. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Associate Professor) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University's School of Business  seeks a faculty member who can contribute not only through excellence in teaching and scholarship, but also through leadership in program development, faculty collaboration, industry engagement, and strategic initiatives. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Philosophy (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The Department of Philosophy and Political Science in the College of Arts & Sciences at Quinnipiac University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The preferred start date is January 2027 or August 2027. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Legal Studies-Emerging Legal Technologies & Civil Procedures (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses, including Civil Procedures, as well as courses aligned with their expertise and program needs. We have a strong preference for candidates with experience teaching and researching innovative and emerging legal technologies, such as artificial intelligence (AI), and who can enhance our curriculum accordingly. Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Quinnipiac University’s School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, 12-month year-round Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work This is an exciting opportunity to join a rapidly growing Master of Social Work (MSW) program committed to preparing competent, socially responsive social workers through flexible, high-quality learning environments. Full-Time Faculty: Sports Communications Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The successful candidate will contribute to a long legacy of excellence in Sports Communications at Quinnipiac and will be at the forefront of the launch of a new, cutting-edge interdisciplinary major in Sports Communications, starting in the Fall 2025 semester. Part-Time Faculty: Philosophy AY 26/27 Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The Philosophy program of Quinnipiac University seeks highly qualified applicants who are committed to excellence in teaching on-ground for part-time faculty openings for the AY 26/27 school year. Part-Time Faculty: Chemistry AY 26/27 Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The Department of Chemistry and Physical Sciences in the College of Arts and Sciences of Quinnipiac University invites applications for part-time faculty to teach entry level on-ground lab courses in general Chemistry for academic year 2026-2027.\n\nOpenings are in day-time sections teaching the following courses:  General Chemistry I Lab (CHE110L) and General Chemistry II Lab (CHE111L). Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: School of Law North Haven - North Haven, CT We are especially interested in candidates who can contribute to our Legal Research and Writing program while also teaching in a foundational doctrinal area. This integrated teaching model reflects the School’s commitment to combining skills instruction, doctrinal learning, and bar readiness. Part-Time Faculty: Physics Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The Department of Chemistry and Physical Sciences of Quinnipiac University seeks highly qualified applicants who are committed to excellence in teaching for a part-time faculty opening to teach introductory physics courses during the Fall 2026 semester. We have openings for PHY101 (Elements of Physics) laboratory and PHY110 (General Physics 1) lecture and laboratory courses. Full-Time Clinical Faculty: Physical Therapy (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Quinnipiac University's School of Health Sciences invites applications for  a full-time, open-rank, clinical core faculty to develop and serve within the CAPTE accredited Quinnipiac University Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) program Part-Time Faculty: School of Business - Finance Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University seeks highly qualified applicants who are committed to excellence in teaching for on-ground part-time faculty opportunities in the Department of Finance within the School of Business on our Mt. Carmel Campus in Hamden, CT with an expected start date of Fall 2026. Full-Time Visiting Faculty: Industrial Engineering Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT We are seeking candidates who share this passion to join the faculty in a full-time visiting faculty position beginning in Fall 2026. This is a benefits-eligible position. Part-Time Faculty: Industrial Engineering and General Engineering - Spring 2026 Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The School of Computing and Engineering at Quinnipiac University seeks highly qualified applicants who are committed to excellence in teaching for part-time faculty openings in Industrial Engineering for the Spring 2026 semester and beyond. The school is experiencing steady enrollment growth, and both needs candidates immediately and desires to develop and maintain a pool of candidates should additional part-time openings arise. Part-Time Faculty: School of Business - Business Analytics & Information Systems Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University seeks highly qualified applicants who are committed to excellence in teaching for part-time faculty opportunities in the Department of  Business Analytics & Information Systems within the School of Business on our Mt. Carmel Campus in Hamden, CT with an expected start date of Fall 2026. Part-Time Faculty: Civil and Mechanical Engineering - Spring 2025 Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The School of Computing and Engineering at Quinnipiac University seeks highly qualified applicants who are committed to excellence in teaching for part-time faculty openings in Civil and Mechanical Engineering for the Spring 2025 semester and beyond. The school is experiencing steady enrollment growth, and both needs candidates immediately and desires to develop and maintain a pool of candidates should additional part-time openings arise. Position Campus Closes Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Quinnipiac University's School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science at the Department of Diagnostic Imaging.  This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful difference in the lives of future healthcare professionals while working in a collaborative and dynamic university environment. Full-Time Faculty: Health and Exercise Science (Nutrition) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University’s Department of Health and Exercise Science, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for a full-time, 12-month position at the Assistant Professor rank (Tenure-Track or Clinical Track) in the area of human nutrition. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Assistant Professor) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The School of Business at Quinnipiac University invites dynamic, innovative, and student-focused educators to join our Finance Department as a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Finance beginning in Fall 2027. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Finance (Associate Professor) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Quinnipiac University's School of Business  seeks a faculty member who can contribute not only through excellence in teaching and scholarship, but also through leadership in program development, faculty collaboration, industry engagement, and strategic initiatives. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Philosophy (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The Department of Philosophy and Political Science in the College of Arts & Sciences at Quinnipiac University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The preferred start date is January 2027 or August 2027. Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Legal Studies-Emerging Legal Technologies & Civil Procedures (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses, including Civil Procedures, as well as courses aligned with their expertise and program needs. We have a strong preference for candidates with experience teaching and researching innovative and emerging legal technologies, such as artificial intelligence (AI), and who can enhance our curriculum accordingly. Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Quinnipiac University’s School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, 12-month year-round Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work This is an exciting opportunity to join a rapidly growing Master of Social Work (MSW) program committed to preparing competent, socially responsive social workers through flexible, high-quality learning environments. Full-Time Faculty: Sports Communications Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The successful candidate will contribute to a long legacy of excellence in Sports Communications at Quinnipiac and will be at the forefront of the launch of a new, cutting-edge interdisciplinary major in Sports Communications, starting in the Fall 2025 semester. Part-Time Faculty: Philosophy AY 26/27 Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT The Philosophy program of Quinnipiac University 