      "title": "Explore Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Explore Careers | Working at Quinnipiac University Search is currently not available. A Quinnipiac Education Academics Undergraduate Graduate Medicine Law Apply Now Visit Contact Us Life at Quinnipiac Student Experience Quinnipiac Now Athletics & Recreation Admissions Admissions Apply Now Tuition & Financial Aid Meet Us Visit Us Virtual Tour Contact Us On Campus Maps & Directions Our Campuses University Calendar University Directory About Quinnipiac Explore Videos Student Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog University Policies Health & Campus Safety Course Finder MyQ Other Resources Alumni Career Development Office Institutes & Centers Ireland's Great Hunger Museum Make a Tuition Payment News Media Parents QCard Quinnipiac University Online Quinnipiac University Poll Quinnipiac Magazine Request a Transcript Student Consumer Information WQUN Working at Quinnipiac Schools Arts & Sciences Business Communications Education Engineering Health Sciences Law Medicine Nursing Looking for a specific program? Program Listing Dual-Degree Programs Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Carret icon Explore Careers Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Application Process Benefits Community Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science (12-month) Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497278 Type: Full-time Campus: North Haven - North Haven, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: Quinnipiac University's School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science at the Department of Diagnostic Imaging. This is a 12-month, year-round appointment that provides leadership and oversight of the clinical education component of the program, ensuring high-quality students’ clinical experiences, establishing, and maintaining strong clinical partnerships, student achievement of clinical competencies, and ongoing compliance with accreditation standards. This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful difference in the lives of future healthcare professionals while working in a collaborative and dynamic university environment.  Application review will start immediately until the position is filled. About the School/Program: The School of Health Sciences is home to approximately 100 full-time faculty and staff and enrolls over 2,500 students across 30 graduate and undergraduate academic programs. The school is organized into seven departments offering undergraduate majors in biomedical sciences, diagnostic medical sonography, exercise science, health science studies, medical microbiology & immunology and radiologic sciences, and graduate programs in advanced medical imagining & leadership, biomedical sciences, cardiovascular perfusion, occupational therapy, pathologists’ assistant, physician assistant, physical therapy and social work. The school also offers entry-level dual-degrees for occupational therapy, physician assistant and physical therapy. Our school provides excellence in education, scholarship, and community engagement with a mission grounded in our commitment to producing skilled and compassionate graduates, pioneering research and partnering with our communities to advance the health and well-being of all individuals. Through unique and distinctive academic programs, interdisciplinary collaboration, immersive learning experiences, and student-centeredness, we empower students to deliver compassionate care, create innovation through research, and catalyze change in dynamic health fields. Our emphasis on evidence-based medicine, critical thinking, and interprofessional healthcare skills equips our graduates to make impactful and inclusive contributions to their professions. In all our endeavors, we are guided by a commitment to innovation, accountability, excellence, and social responsibility as we aspire to be a first-choice school of excellence and a global leader in fostering new knowledge, improving healthcare, and increasing health equity. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 22 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles — including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men’s ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Support mission, vision, core values, and strategic plans of Quinnipiac University,  and the  School of Health Sciences. Coordinate the clinical education component of the Radiologic Sciences Program in collaboration with the Program Director, and in compliance with JRCERT accreditation requirements. Ensure integration of clinical education with didactic and laboratory instruction. Develop, implement, and evaluate clinical education policies, procedures, competencies, and assessment processes. Serve as the primary liaison between the program and clinical education sites. Coordinate student clinical assignments, rotations, and scheduling. Conduct clinical site visits and evaluate educational quality. Monitor student clinical performance, competency attainment, and professional behaviors. Maintain accurate clinical education records and competency documentation. Assist with clinical instructor orientation, training, and evaluation. Support JRCERT accreditation activities and outcomes assessment. Teach assigned didactic, laboratory, and/or clinical courses. Support student success, retention, and on-time graduation through participation in advising, recruitment, retention, service, department, school and institutional events. Perform additional responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair. Education Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Radiologic Science or related field from an accredited institution. Current ARRT certification and registration in Radiography. Eligibility for Connecticut licensure. Minimum of two years of full-time clinical radiography experience. Minimum of one year of teaching experience in a JRCERT-accredited radiography program or equivalent clinical instruction experience. Knowledge of clinical education, competency-based assessment, and accreditation standards. Strong organizational, communication, and collaborative skills. Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in TED field from an accredited institution Prior experience as a Clinical Coordinator or Director of Clinical Education ARRT post-primary credential(s) Experience with JRCERT accreditation and outcomes assessment Experience with distance, hybrid, or alternative instructional modalities Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a resume, a cover letter detailing how your experience aligns with the position requirements, demonstrated commitment to intentional leadership that values individuals of all backgrounds and experiences, and contact information for three references. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: September 02, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great. We can send you jobs like this. if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search Results Position Campus Closes Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Open until filled Quinnipiac University's School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science at the Department of Diagnostic Imaging.  This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful difference in the lives of future healthcare professionals while working in a collaborative and dynamic university environment. Position Campus Closes Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Open until filled Quinnipiac University's School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, open-rank, Clinical Assistant Professor & Clinical Director of Radiologic Science at the Department of Diagnostic Imaging.  This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful difference in the lives of future healthcare professionals while working in a collaborative and dynamic university environment. Powered by PageUp Already Applied? Complete your application, submit your application, or view the status of an application. Login Search Refine Search Type Full-time 1 Campus North Haven - North Haven, CT 1 Categories Faculty 1 Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Quinnipiac Home About Quinnipiac https://www.facebook.com/QuinnipiacUniversity http://twitter.com/quinnipiacu https://instagram.com/quinnipiacu © 2020 Quinnipiac University. All Rights Reserved. Website Security and Privacy Policy Legal Info"
