    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497277/fulltime-faculty-health-and-exercise-science-nutrition": {
      "title": "Explore Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Explore Careers | Working at Quinnipiac University Search is currently not available. A Quinnipiac Education Academics Undergraduate Graduate Medicine Law Apply Now Visit Contact Us Life at Quinnipiac Student Experience Quinnipiac Now Athletics & Recreation Admissions Admissions Apply Now Tuition & Financial Aid Meet Us Visit Us Virtual Tour Contact Us On Campus Maps & Directions Our Campuses University Calendar University Directory About Quinnipiac Explore Videos Student Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog University Policies Health & Campus Safety Course Finder MyQ Other Resources Alumni Career Development Office Institutes & Centers Ireland's Great Hunger Museum Make a Tuition Payment News Media Parents QCard Quinnipiac University Online Quinnipiac University Poll Quinnipiac Magazine Request a Transcript Student Consumer Information WQUN Working at Quinnipiac Schools Arts & Sciences Business Communications Education Engineering Health Sciences Law Medicine Nursing Looking for a specific program? Program Listing Dual-Degree Programs Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Carret icon Explore Careers Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Application Process Benefits Community Full-Time Faculty: Health and Exercise Science (Nutrition) Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497277 Type: Full-time Campus: Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: Quinnipiac University’s Department of Health and Exercise Science, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for a full-time, 12-month faculty position at the  rank of Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track or Clinical Track) in the area of human nutrition. The ideal candidate is an educator who will be integral in teaching our nutrition courses and further develop the current programs that emphasize the vital role of food and nutrition in maintaining healthy lifestyles, athletic performance, medical nutrition therapy, and promoting community wellness. The successful applicant will aid our pursuit of organizing a shared learning community and contribute to the education of students in the challenges of understanding nutrition, exercise, health and wellness, population health, health equity, and public health; developing and building a strong culture of health and wellness among faculty, students, and staff; foster a student-centered environment by delivering engaging and innovative coursework; being accessible, approachable, and relatable to students;  display passion, energy, and excitement in health and exercise sciences for our students; be an innovative educator who can excel in the traditional classroom and laboratory settings, with occasional hybrid or online modalities at the undergraduate level when needed; be able to participate in interdisciplinary collaboration that engage and educate students who plan to provide direct patient/client care and in public health. This is an on-ground position. The search committee will start reviewing applications immediately, and the expected start date will be in January 2027. About the School/Program: The School of Health Sciences is home to approximately 100 full-time faculty and professional staff and enrolls over 2120 students across over 22 graduate and undergraduate academic offerings. The school is organized into 7 departments offering undergraduate majors in biomedical sciences, health sciences, radiologic sciences, medical microbiology & Immunology and diagnostic medical sonography and graduate majors in physician assistant studies, occupational therapy, physical therapy, social work, biomedical sciences, pathologists’ assistant and cardiovascular perfusion. Our school provides excellence in education, scholarship, and community engagement with a mission grounded in our commitment to producing skilled and compassionate graduates, creating pioneering research, and partnering with our communities to advance the health and well-being of people and communities. Through unique and distinctive academic programs, interdisciplinary collaboration, immersive learning experiences, and student-centeredness that we empower students to deliver compassionate care, create innovation through research, and catalyze change in dynamic health fields. Our emphasis on evidence-based medicine, critical thinking, and interprofessional skills equips our graduates to make impactful and inclusive contributions to their professions. In all our endeavors, we are guided by a commitment to innovation, accountability, excellence, and social responsibility as we aspire to be a first-choice school of excellence and a global leader in fostering new knowledge, improving healthcare, and increasing health equity. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 22 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles - including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men's ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Support the mission, vision, values, and strategic goals of Quinnipiac University and the School of Health Sciences, and the Department of Health and Exercise Science Teach classes assigned by department chair Support curriculum development and evaluation Serve as an academic advisor and mentor to students Participate in faculty development activities Participate in professional activities within and beyond School of Health Science to maximize student learning, faculty scholarship, and programmatic effectiveness Participate in student recruitment and retention activities Collaborate with faculty colleagues in teaching and research Support experiential learning and community engagement initiatives Contribute to curriculum development and innovation Support the School of Health Science and University’s vision, mission, core values and work to implement our strategic plans Provide service to the Department, SHS, QU, and the community Actively participate in the School of Health Science community In Addition, for Tenure-Track Appointment : Maintain an active research agenda, external grant applications and outputs with publications in high-quality journals in the discipline. Education Requirements: Required: Clinical Track: Master's degree (M.S. or M.P.H.) in dietetics, clinical nutrition, food and nutrition, or a related field. Tenure-Track: Doctor of Clinical Nutrition (DCN) or Ph.D. in Nutrition, or a closely related field. Preferred: Doctor of Clinical Nutrition (DCN), Ph.D. in Nutrition, post-professional or research doctoral degree in closely related field awarded by an institution accredited by a regional accrediting agency, which recognized by the U.S. Department of Education. Tenure-Track: Post-Doctorate experience and track record of external grant applications and/or awards. Qualifications: Required: Registered Dietitian Nutritionist (RDN) Independent teaching experience at the undergraduate level. Evidence of strong teaching skills and the use of instructional technology. Professional working experience in nutrition & dietetics. Commitment to community engagement and professional advocacy through teaching, service, and scholarship. For tenure track: Evidence of ability to establish a scholarly agenda (e.g., scholarship of application, discovery, integration, or teaching) through peer-reviewed publication, presentations, and ongoing research outputs and external grant applications. Preferred: Commission on Dietetic Registration (CDR) certificated specialization. At least 2 years of clinical experience in nutrition. Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically by including cover letter detailing your experience aligns with the position requirements, describing your interest in and qualifications for the role, including but not limited to your teaching, clinical experience, research, and external grant applications; curriculum vitae; teaching philosophy statement, addressing how to engage students from across academic programs (within and beyond Quinnipiac University School of Health Sciences), and ideas on integrating experiential learning into your teaching; Contact information for three professional references (on the application form). For Tenure-Track: Research agenda, published manuscripts or other evidence of scholarly outputs. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: September 02, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great. We can send you jobs like this. if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search Results Position Campus Closes Full-Time Faculty: Health and Exercise Science (Nutrition) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Open until filled Quinnipiac University’s Department of Health and Exercise Science, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for a full-time, 12-month position at the Assistant Professor rank (Tenure-Track or Clinical Track) in the area of human nutrition. Position Campus Closes Full-Time Faculty: Health and Exercise Science (Nutrition) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Open until filled Quinnipiac University’s Department of Health and Exercise Science, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for a full-time, 12-month position at the Assistant Professor rank (Tenure-Track or Clinical Track) in the area of human nutrition. Powered by PageUp Already Applied? Complete your application, submit your application, or view the status of an application. Login Search Refine Search Type Full-time 1 Campus Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT 1 Categories Faculty 1 Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Quinnipiac Home About Quinnipiac https://www.facebook.com/QuinnipiacUniversity http://twitter.com/quinnipiacu https://instagram.com/quinnipiacu © 2020 Quinnipiac University. All Rights Reserved. Website Security and Privacy Policy Legal Info"
