    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497323/fulltime-tenure-track-faculty-philosophy-college-of-arts-sciences": {
      "title": "Explore Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Explore Careers | Working at Quinnipiac University Search is currently not available. A Quinnipiac Education Academics Undergraduate Graduate Medicine Law Apply Now Visit Contact Us Life at Quinnipiac Student Experience Quinnipiac Now Athletics & Recreation Admissions Admissions Apply Now Tuition & Financial Aid Meet Us Visit Us Virtual Tour Contact Us On Campus Maps & Directions Our Campuses University Calendar University Directory About Quinnipiac Explore Videos Student Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog University Policies Health & Campus Safety Course Finder MyQ Other Resources Alumni Career Development Office Institutes & Centers Ireland's Great Hunger Museum Make a Tuition Payment News Media Parents QCard Quinnipiac University Online Quinnipiac University Poll Quinnipiac Magazine Request a Transcript Student Consumer Information WQUN Working at Quinnipiac Schools Arts & Sciences Business Communications Education Engineering Health Sciences Law Medicine Nursing Looking for a specific program? Program Listing Dual-Degree Programs Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Carret icon Explore Careers Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Application Process Benefits Community Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Philosophy (College of Arts & Sciences) Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497323 Type: Full-time Campus: Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: The Department of Philosophy and Political Science in the College of Arts & Sciences at Quinnipiac University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The preferred start date is August 2027. We seek a dynamic and collaborative teacher-scholar committed to excellence in undergraduate teaching and scholarly engagement. The successful candidate will teach core Philosophy courses and contribute to the continued development of innovative offerings that serve students across a range of academic disciplines, particularly in areas of sustained and growing demand such as ethics, artificial intelligence, bioethics, environmental ethics, human rights, criminal justice and law. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued evolution of Philosophy's curricular offerings and its interdisciplinary support of programs across the University. We seek a colleague who will help refresh and modernize the curriculum through innovative teaching and course development in areas of emerging importance and student demand. Philosophy plays an important role in undergraduate instruction and interdisciplinary support across the University. The Philosophy program currently offers 20 courses that serve the general education curriculum, enrolling over 400 students annually in core introductory courses: Introduction to Philosophy, ethics, and logic. These enrollments reflect sustained student demand. Philosophy also provides essential coursework supporting numerous programs, including Nursing and Health Sciences (Bioethics), Environmental Studies (Environmental Ethics), Political Science (Human Rights; War and Peace), Computer Science (Ethics and AI), Sports Studies (Philosophy of Sport), History, and Women’s and Gender Studies (Philosophy of Feminism). We also support the university honors program and offer courses that provide University Certificates. The department supports a Philosophy minor and a Certificate in 21st‑Century Ethical Problems, both of which attract students from a wide range of majors. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a commitment to interdisciplinary education, experiential learning, and community engagement, preparing students for future success in their lives and careers. About the College: The College of Arts & Sciences is a vibrant and inclusive community dedicated to providing an immersive and distinctive educational experience. Known for our inclusive teaching, faculty mentorship, and high-impact experiences, our programs integrate career planning and skill development into a broad education tailored to meet the needs and challenges of the 21st century. Our students emerge as ethical and intellectual leaders, capable of critical and independent thinking, equipped to collaborate on solutions to pressing global issues, and prepared for success in their personal, professional, and civic lives. The College of Arts & Sciences offers 25 undergraduate majors, 34 undergraduate minors, an MS in Molecular and Cell Biology, 6 undergraduate and 1 graduate certificates, and 13 undergraduate/graduate dual-degree programs. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing, and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 22 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles — including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men’s ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation, and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Teach courses to meet departmental and programmatic needs (e.g. Introduction to Philosophy, Introduction to Ethics, Environmental Philosophy, History of Western Philosophy). The standard teaching load for research-active tenure-track faculty is 3 courses (9 credits) per semester. Integrate engaging, inclusive, and innovative pedagogies and experiences to enhance student learning and engagement Maintain an active research program that will engage students and lead to scholarly presentations and publications Demonstrate a willingness to communicate information about their area of expertise on campus and in the wider community Advise and mentor undergraduate students and philosophy-related student organizations and activities Foster a supportive and inclusive community in which everyone belongs Engage in appropriate departmental, college, university, professional, and/or public service as relevant to the position Education Requirements: PhD in Philosophy or a related field by the time of appointment, with demonstrated academic preparation and teaching competence in Philosophy. ABD candidates who expect to complete their degree before the start date are encouraged to apply. Qualifications: Demonstrated ability to conduct and publish research in the discipline and engage in public scholarship where appropriate. Excellent verbal and written communication skills Demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of an interdisciplinary team Ability to integrate experiential learning modalities Additional Information This is an on ground in-person position. Candidates must be able to work regularly at Quinnipiac University’s Mount Carmel campus and be willing to relocate within a reasonable commuting distance, if applicable. Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Review of applications will begin October 5, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Application Instructions: Please submit the following documents: Cover letter that addresses the following: qualifications for the position Approach to instruction and equity-minded teaching practices Experience and approach to working both independently and with teams C.V. Statement of teaching philosophy, addressing how to engage students from across academic programs and ideas around integrating experiential learning Names, e-mail addresses and phone numbers of three professional references who will not be contacted without the candidate’s prior approval We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: August 25, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great. We can send you jobs like this. if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search Results Position Campus Closes Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Philosophy (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Open until filled The Department of Philosophy and Political Science in the College of Arts & Sciences at Quinnipiac University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The preferred start date is January 2027 or August 2027. Position Campus Closes Full-Time Tenure Track Faculty: Philosophy (College of Arts & Sciences) Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT Open until filled The Department of Philosophy and Political Science in the College of Arts & Sciences at Quinnipiac University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor. The preferred start date is January 2027 or August 2027. Powered by PageUp Already Applied? Complete your application, submit your application, or view the status of an application. Login Search Refine Search Type Full-time 1 Campus Mount Carmel - Hamden, CT 1 Categories Faculty 1 Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Quinnipiac Home About Quinnipiac https://www.facebook.com/QuinnipiacUniversity http://twitter.com/quinnipiacu https://instagram.com/quinnipiacu © 2020 Quinnipiac University. All Rights Reserved. Website Security and Privacy Policy Legal Info"
