    "https://career.qu.edu/en-us/job/497279/clinical-assistant-professor-of-social-work-12month": {
      "title": "Explore Job Opportunities",
      "description": "Explore Careers | Working at Quinnipiac University Search is currently not available. A Quinnipiac Education Academics Undergraduate Graduate Medicine Law Apply Now Visit Contact Us Life at Quinnipiac Student Experience Quinnipiac Now Athletics & Recreation Admissions Admissions Apply Now Tuition & Financial Aid Meet Us Visit Us Virtual Tour Contact Us On Campus Maps & Directions Our Campuses University Calendar University Directory About Quinnipiac Explore Videos Student Resources Academic Calendar Academic Catalog University Policies Health & Campus Safety Course Finder MyQ Other Resources Alumni Career Development Office Institutes & Centers Ireland's Great Hunger Museum Make a Tuition Payment News Media Parents QCard Quinnipiac University Online Quinnipiac University Poll Quinnipiac Magazine Request a Transcript Student Consumer Information WQUN Working at Quinnipiac Schools Arts & Sciences Business Communications Education Engineering Health Sciences Law Medicine Nursing Looking for a specific program? Program Listing Dual-Degree Programs Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Carret icon Explore Careers Working at Quinnipiac Explore Job Opportunities Application Process Benefits Community Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work (12-month) Apply now Back to search results Job Number: 497279 Type: Full-time Campus: North Haven - North Haven, CT Categories: Faculty Overview: Quinnipiac University’s School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, 12-month year-round Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work This is an exciting opportunity to join a rapidly growing Master of Social Work (MSW) program committed to preparing competent, socially responsive social workers through flexible, high-quality learning environments. The successful candidate will serve as a principal faculty member with primary responsibilities in teaching and advising in the on-campus and/or online program formats along with service. Candidates are expected to be on campus for a minimum of three days per week. We encourage candidates who are licensed social workers with relevant experience and qualifications to apply. The search committee will start reviewing applications immediately, and the expected start date will be in January 2027. About the School/Program: The School of Health Sciences is home to approximately 100 full-time faculty and staff and enrolls over 2,500 students across 30 graduate and undergraduate academic programs. The school is organized into seven departments offering undergraduate majors in biomedical sciences, diagnostic medical sonography, exercise science, health science studies, medical microbiology & immunology and radiologic sciences, and graduate programs in advanced medical imagining & leadership, biomedical sciences, cardiovascular perfusion, occupational therapy, pathologists’ assistant, physician assistant, physical therapy and social work. The school also offers entry-level dual-degrees for occupational therapy, physician assistant and physical therapy. Our school provides excellence in education, scholarship, and community engagement with a mission grounded in our commitment to producing skilled and compassionate graduates, pioneering research and partnering with our communities to advance the health and well-being of all individuals. Through unique and distinctive academic programs, interdisciplinary collaboration, immersive learning experiences, and student-centeredness, we empower students to deliver compassionate care, create innovation through research, and catalyze change in dynamic health fields. Our emphasis on evidence-based medicine, critical thinking, and interprofessional healthcare skills equips our graduates to make impactful and inclusive contributions to their professions. In all our endeavors, we are guided by a commitment to innovation, accountability, excellence, and social responsibility as we aspire to be a first-choice school of excellence and a global leader in fostering new knowledge, improving healthcare, and increasing health equity. About Quinnipiac: Quinnipiac University is a private, coeducational institution located 90 minutes north of New York City and two hours from Boston. The university currently has an enrollment of 9,700 students in more than 100-degree programs through its Schools of Business, Communications, Computing & Engineering, Education, Health Sciences, Law, Medicine, Nursing and the College of Arts & Sciences. Our 22 Division I teams have achieved remarkable success, boasting national and conference titles — including a 2023 NCAA national championship win in men’s ice hockey, a trip to the Sweet 16 for our women's basketball team and NCAA Tournament appearances by many of our programs. The Quinnipiac University Poll is nationally recognized as a leader in public opinion research, and the university is consistently recognized by U.S. News & World Report and Princeton Review. The Wall Street Journal ranked Quinnipiac #51 among the best colleges in the nation, and second in Connecticut, for our exceptional graduation rate, salary impact, learning facilities, career preparation and learning opportunities. The university is in the midst of program expansion and renewal for both traditional and adult learners, the development of innovative strategic partnerships, and recently opened South Quad with three state-of-the-art buildings. As Quinnipiac grows, the university remains guided by the core values that define our community and shapes the experience of every student and employee. We are fiercely committed to ensuring every Bobcat thrives. We are a lifelong partner for every learner. We passionately care about our community. Everyone should feel welcome and valued. We boldly shape our university's future. We will forge a path of impact together. These values are the foundation of who we are and reflect the Quinnipiac spirit found across our campuses. For more information, please visit qu.edu. Connect with Quinnipiac on Facebook, Instagram, YouTube, TikTok and X. Responsibilities: Support the mission, vision, values, and strategic goals of Quinnipiac University and the School of Health Sciences, and the Department of Social Work Teach courses across the generalist and specialized MSW curriculum in online and/or on-campus formats, based on program needs Advise and mentor MSW students, including monitoring academic progress, professional development, and competency attainment Participate in all department-required faculty activities, in addition to department, school, and university service Participate in student recruitment and program events (e.g., welcome weekend, admitted students’ weekends, and open houses) Perform additional responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair and/or Associate Chair and/or Associate Director, Online MSW Education Requirements: Master of Social Work degree from a CSWE accredited institution in the United States. Qualifications: Minimum of two years post MSW social work practice MSW or BSW online (asynchronous, synchronous) and in-person teaching experience Social Work State Licensure (LMSW/LCSW) Willingness to develop and build MSW courses Proven ability to collaborate effectively with individuals from varied backgrounds Preferred Qualifications: Doctorate degree in social work or related field, from a regionally accredited institution Full-time MSW online (asynchronous, synchronous) and in-person teaching experience Experience building online MSW courses in Canvas Experience with student advising, retention, and support in online and/or in-person learning environments Leadership experience at the department or program level Interest in higher education leadership, including engagement in program development and academic administration Experience serving as lead faculty to support part-time faculty Proven ability to foster inclusive, equitable environments for teaching, learning and social work practice Scholarship and creative works, particularly related to teaching and learning Special Instructions to Applicants: TO APPLY: Applications must be submitted electronically and include a resume, a cover letter detailing how your experience aligns with the position requirements, demonstrated commitment to intentional leadership that values individuals of all backgrounds and experiences, and contact information for three references(references will not be contacted without permission)  and a statement of teaching philosophy that addresses a commitment to intentional teaching, advising/mentoring in the online and on-ground MSW environment and inclusive excellence. We offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time faculty and staff which includes tuition remission and a culture that is inclusive and driven by excellence. Quinnipiac University is an equal opportunity employer and encourages applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and respectful community. Advertised: August 19, 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great. We can send you jobs like this. if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search Results Position Campus Closes Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Open until filled Quinnipiac University’s School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, 12-month year-round Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work This is an exciting opportunity to join a rapidly growing Master of Social Work (MSW) program committed to preparing competent, socially responsive social workers through flexible, high-quality learning environments. Position Campus Closes Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work (12-month) North Haven - North Haven, CT Open until filled Quinnipiac University’s School of Health Sciences invites applications for a full-time, 12-month year-round Clinical Assistant Professor of Social Work This is an exciting opportunity to join a rapidly growing Master of Social Work (MSW) program committed to preparing competent, socially responsive social workers through flexible, high-quality learning environments. Powered by PageUp Already Applied? Complete your application, submit your application, or view the status of an application. Login Search Refine Search Type Full-time 1 Campus North Haven - North Haven, CT 1 Categories Faculty 1 Job Alerts Subscribe to Job Alerts Quinnipiac Home About Quinnipiac https://www.facebook.com/QuinnipiacUniversity http://twitter.com/quinnipiacu https://instagram.com/quinnipiacu © 2020 Quinnipiac University. All Rights Reserved. Website Security and Privacy Policy Legal Info"
